invisiblebarrier barrier invisible~
   A voice speaks to you from out of Nowhere:

I am Aglandiir, Smiter of Evil andinjustice - Keeper of the Ring of
Murana.  I shall tell you a story.....

   Many millennia ago - before the human race came to the Dominion and
when Kirahn was silent and trapped - locked away by The Lord Moriquendi
in Rigorous Nine...there was a beautiful forest in place of the wasteland
surrounding you now.  It was called Murana and it possessed the most
powerful thing ever: Love and Peace.  The druids walked freely and
the everything was balanced for it was where the Kinnslayer was born.
   But everything was not quite as peaceful and malevolent as it seemed
in Murana, for a great druid of the Kinnslayer became enraged when he was
not picked to be the bearer of the Kinnslayer Amulet and Andara, Garou's
love was.  He left Murana and went into the mountains east of the forest.
They are known as Thangorodrim.  No one had ever ventured into the orc
filled mountains ever and returned.  Melkor Bagollith was never seen again
until....
   Strange things began to happen in Murana.  Black flaming beasts began
coming from Thangorodrim - beasts whose power and evil nature had never
been seen since Kirahn ruled The Dominion.  They killed and pillaged the
inhabitants of the forest brutally and without mercy.  They wielded
whips of fire which burned the sacred trees.  And Melkor returned himself
and cast a black spell which began to poison Murana.  The trees died
and the forest druids fled to Darkweir.  Only one man stepped forth to
stop Melkor.  His name was Darkshade.  

  Darkshade collected the kings of the Lands of the Dominion and led
them upon flying dragons into Thangorodrim.  A great war ensued, Melkor
and his army of Balrogs and the Dreaded Orcs fought the valiant and tiny
army of Dragonriders led by Darkshade.  The war lasted for thousands of
years, and The Dominion began to die.  
   I was young, very young, but brave.  I carried upon my shoulders Darkshade
himself and Jirdidan carried Andara.  We were the only ones alive and in
the heart of Thangorodrim.  We fought and killed the balrogs and orcs
until it was only us and Melkor.  We were still barely enough to win...
   Finally Andara was struck down by a deadly blow to the heart by Melkor's
Grond and the Kinnslayer Amulet.  Garou, enraged by this, took Andara
away and left her with his druids in Darkweir Hallows.  He gave his golden
bow to Darkshade and with it Darkshade killed Melkor.  
   Murana was dead - all that remained was a wasteland filled with the
dead of the war.  Even Garou could not restore the great forest to its
once fabled glory.  But Darkshade built a wonderful, golden city just
west of the wasteland and ruled its gold paved avenues with a wise and kind
heart.  
   Then one day, to the shock of the city dwellers, a black temple arose
from the ground with a Black Star sealing the entrance.  The doors were
flung open suddenly and the black Shadow of Kirahn crept out and 
tarnished the glorious city.  The golden streets turned red with blood 
and no one lived...one of the people slain in the shadow of Kirahn was 
Darkshade.
   Melkor stepped through the entrance and regained his rule over the land.
With him came a truly evil man - Spine.  Spine turned the poisoned city
into a place of thievery and death and named it Charring Cross.
   I, many years older and wiser and much, much stronger, came to avenge
my master, and friend, Darkshade.  I could not do it and was terminally
poisoned...kept alive now by the power of Murana, a small ring carrying
the spirit of the forest within it.  With the ring I made this barrier
which will not allow anyone into Thangorodrim until I am fit to destroy
Melkor and all his evil subjects...

Go now traveller...I must rest and become powerful again so I can return
If you remain good in heart and strong, I will find you and we will go
together into Thangorodrim to bring justice to the world....
Go now and have bring peace to the unfortunate and may the Light
of The Moriquendi and the wisdom of the Kinnslayer ever be with you.
~
S
